# Response headers for Cloudflare Pages / Netlify. Copied into dist/ by
# vite.config.ts's copyHeaders plugin, so `pnpm build` (the build command
# Cloudflare's own Vite detection suggests) ships it, not just `task
# web:build`. tools/web/nginx-nanourl.conf expresses the same policy for a
# self-hosted box, and web/tests/headers.test.ts parses both files and
# compares them per path, which checks that they mirror each other.
#
# Cloudflare Pages applies ALL matching rules and comma-joins a header set
# twice, so without `! Cache-Control`, `/*`'s `Cache-Control: no-cache` would
# prepend onto the immutable rules below ("no-cache, public,
# max-age=31536000, immutable"). RFC 9111 §5.2.2.4: no-cache is not cancelled
# by max-age or immutable; the response must be revalidated before every
# reuse, which would make the content-hashed chunks uncacheable. `! Header`
# is Cloudflare's documented remedy: clear what the broader rule set, then
# set our own.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/assets/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

